<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali ibn Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1471">1471</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Moulay Ali ibn Rashid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali ibn Rashid was a sharif of the Banu Rashid who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chefchaouen">Chefchaouen</a> in the Rif mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> in 1471. He built it as a fortified base for holy war against the Portuguese enclaves around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ksar-es-seghir">Ksar es-Seghir</a>, and it became a refuge for Muslims and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>.</p></div>
